Id: 5
Created: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 09:20:23 -0400
Name: Receiving "cannot find Could not find activesupport-8.1.3, bigdecimal-4.1.2 in locally installed gems Run bundle install" despite rubyopt cleaning
Summary: Running a ready'd cli produced that error when run in a dir containing a Gemfile. Some context:
+ 
+ ```zsh
+ # zed -f ready_rstore
+ 
+ ...
+ 
+ 'Warning\[:experimental\]\ \=\ false'
+ 'gemfile\ \=\ File.expand_path\(\"../Gemfile\",\ __dir__\)'
+ 
+ ''
+ 'if\ File.exist\?\(gemfile\)'
+ '\ \ ENV\[\"BUNDLE_GEMFILE\"\]\ \|\|\=\ gemfile'
+ '\ \ require\ \"bundler/setup\"'
+ 'end'
+ 
+ ...
+ ```
+ 
+ 1. ready is currently breaking if bundler/setup is required within the ruby portion of the shim, even though it cleans RUBYOPT
+ 2. binding.irb shows that __dir__ is being evaluated to a directory completely unrelated to this CLI. __dir__ is being evaluated to workdir, rather than a fixed dir, and there happens to be a Gemfile at ../Gemfile relative to my current workdir
Status: open
